1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,290
It sounds like something from the realms of science fiction – a space expedition into the vast expanse of space, heading towards the Red Planet.
这听起来像是科幻小说里的情节——一场深入浩瀚太空的星际探险，目标直指那颗红色星球。

2
00:00:10,290 --> 00:00:19,430
While we’re not quite ready to put a person on terra firma, the question we ask today is: why are so many countries interested in going to Mars?
尽管我们还没准备好将人类送上火星表面，但今天我们要探讨的问题是：为什么这么多国家都对火星探索抱有浓厚兴趣？

3
00:00:19,430 --> 00:00:25,250
The space race saw the USA and USSR compete to achieve firsts in spaceflight.
在太空竞赛时期，美国和苏联曾争相创造航天领域的多个“第一”。

4
00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:33,760
The Soviet Union released Sputnik 1, an artificial satellite, before anyone else, and the US landed on the Moon first.
苏联率先发射了人类第一颗人造卫星“斯普特尼克1号”，而美国则率先实现了载人登月。

5
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:38,370
Now it appears that Mars is the celestial body of desire.
如今，火星似乎成了众望所归的探索目标。

6
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:46,740
While the kudos and bragging rights to be the first nation to touchdown is an obvious draw, there are other reasons we want to get there.
成为首个登陆火星的国家所带来的荣誉与吹嘘的资本，显然是一大吸引力，但我们探索火星还有其他原因。

7
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:50,380
One of these could be the survival of our species.
其中之一可能关乎人类物种的延续。

8
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:58,180
You only have to look at the fossilised remains of the dinosaurs to see the benefit of finding another habitable planet.
只需看看恐龙的化石残骸，就能明白找到另一颗宜居星球的重要意义。

9
00:00:58,180 --> 00:01:09,200
While Mars doesn’t have the right conditions to call it home just yet, there’s always the concept of terraforming – changing the environment of a planet to suit our needs.
虽然火星目前还不具备供人类定居的条件，但“地球化改造”的构想始终存在——也就是改造行星的环境，使其满足人类的生存需求。

10
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:12,430
However, not everyone agrees.
但并非所有人都认同这一构想。

11
00:01:12,430 --> 00:01:26,670
Leading astrophysicist Neil deGrasse Tyson has said the concept of altering habitability of another planet because of the damage we have done to Earth makes no sense when we can simply terraform Earth.
顶尖天体物理学家尼尔·德格拉斯·泰森就曾表示，既然我们完全可以对地球进行生态改造，那么因人类对地球造成了破坏，就去改造另一颗行星使其宜居的想法，根本毫无道理。

12
00:01:26,670 --> 00:01:31,760
It seems the main reason at the moment is the search for extraterrestrial life.
目前来看，探索火星的主要原因似乎是为了寻找外星生命。

13
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:36,570
It has long been believed that, at one time, Mars was abundant with life.
长期以来，人们一直认为火星曾生机勃勃。

14
00:01:36,570 --> 00:01:43,930
Now seemingly dead, the potential fossils could answer questions about our own evolution and that of our planet.
如今这颗星球看似一片死寂，但可能存在的化石，或许能解答关于人类及地球自身进化的诸多疑问。

15
00:01:43,930 --> 00:01:51,550
One theory is that bacterial life on our planet didn’t start here, but was transferred via asteroid from Mars.
有一种理论认为，地球上的细菌生命并非起源于地球，而是通过小行星从火星传播而来的。

16
00:01:51,550 --> 00:02:02,150
One benefit championed by scientists like Neil deGrasse Tyson is that landing on Mars may inspire more people to become interested in science and astronomy.
尼尔·德格拉斯·泰森等科学家推崇的一点是，登陆火星或许能激发更多人对科学和天文学的兴趣。

17
00:02:02,150 --> 00:02:07,570
Surely inspiring a new generation to visit the stars is reason enough.
显然，激励新一代人去探索星辰大海，这本身就已是足够充分的理由。
